  "question": {
    "text": "In a first order decomposition reaction, the time taken for the decomposition of reactant to one fourth and one eighth of its initial concentration are $t_1$ and $t_2(s)$, respectively. The ratio $t_1 / t_2$ will :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $\\mathrm{I}^{\\text {st }}$ order reaction<br />When $\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{t}}=\\mathrm{Co} / 4$<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& \\mathrm{t}_1=2 \\mathrm{t}_{50 \\%}. \\\\<br>& \\text { when } \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{t}}=\\mathrm{Co} / 8 \\\\<br>& \\mathrm{t}_2=3 \\mathrm{t}_{50 \\%} \\\\<br>& \\text { so } \\frac{\\mathrm{t}_1}{\\mathrm{t}_2}=\\frac{2}{3}<br />\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}